WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
A change in sediment supply or depositional conditions creates

2
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:07.780 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
a different layer. Bedding records these changes. Read the

3
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.220 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
boundaries and the material inside each bed before interpreting

4
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:16.040 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
the sequence. A sediment-bearing flow weakens. Coarser grains settle

5
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.560 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
first, then finer particles accumulate above them. The resulting

6
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.800 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
bed fines upward. This is a graded bed; it

7
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.760 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
records a change during deposition within one bed. Wind

8
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.600 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
or water carries grains up a bedform and deposits

9
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.280 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
them on the down-current slope. The bedform moves while

10
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.940 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
inclined laminae accumulate and are partly truncated. These are

11
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.560 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
cross beds. They record deposition and migration, not a

12
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.840 line:0% position:50% size:94% align:center
later fold of every layer.
